\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 A titan is about 25 feet tall and weighs about 14,000 pounds. 
\par Titans speak Abyssal, Common, Celestial, Draconic, and Giant.
\par }{COMBAT
\par }{\fs20 A titan\rquote s natural weapons, as well as any weapons it wields, are treated as chaotic-aligned for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction. 
\par }{\b\fs20 Oversized Weapon (Ex):}{\fs20  A titan wields a great, two-handed warhammer (big enough for Gargantuan creatures) without penalty.
\par }{\b\fs20 Spell-Like Abilities: }{\fs20 At will\emdash }{\i\fs20 chain lightning }{\fs20 (DC 23), }{\i\fs20 charm monster }{\fs20 (DC 21), }{\i\fs20 cure critical wounds }{\fs20 (DC 21), }{\i\fs20 fire storm }{\fs20 (DC 24), }{\i\fs20 
greater dispel magic, hold monster }{\fs20 (DC 22), }{\i\fs20 invisibility, invisibility purge, levitate, persistent image }{\fs20 (DC 22), }{\i\fs20 polymorph }{\fs20 (humanoid forms only, duration 1 hour); 3/day\emdash }{\i\fs20 
etherealness, word of chaos }{\fs20 (DC 22), }{\i\fs20 summon nature\rquote s ally IX}{\fs20 ; 1/day\emdash }{\i\fs20 gate, maze, meteor swarm }{\fs20 (DC 26). Caster level 20th. The save DCs are Charisma-based. 
\par In addition, titans of good or neutral alignment can use the following additional spell-like abilities: At will\emdash }{\i\fs20 daylight, holy smite }{\fs20 (DC 21), }{\i\fs20 remove curse }{\fs20 (DC 21); 1/day\emdash }{\i\fs20 greater restoration}{
\fs20 . Caster level 20th. The save DCs are Charisma-based.
\par Titans of evil alignment can use the following additional spell-like abilities: At will\emdash }{\i\fs20 bestow curse }{\fs20 (DC 21), }{\i\fs20 deeper darkness, unholy blight }{\fs20 (DC 21); 1/day\emdash }{\i\fs20 crushing hand }{\fs20 
(DC 26). Caster level 20th. The save DCs are Charisma-based.
\par }{TACTICS ROUND-BY-ROUND
\par }{\fs20 Titans enjoy combat and usually close with their foes. If that proves ineffective, they swiftly back off and pelt the foe with spell-like abilities and magical effects. Because of a titan\rquote s Quicken Spell-Like Ability feat, it can use }{
\i\fs20 chain lightning }{\fs20 as a free action, and frequently attacks in melee while lashing out with this ability at the same time.
\par }{\i\fs20 Prior to combat: Invisibility purge }{\fs20 or }{\i\fs20 invisibility}{\fs20 .
\par }{\i\fs20 Round 1: }{\fs20 Charge and attempt to sunder the weapon of the most dangerous foe. Hurl }{\i\fs20 chain lightning }{\fs20 at opponents standing away from the fight.
\par }{\i\fs20 Round 2: }{\fs20 Full attack against the disarmed opponent, and hurl }{\i\fs20 chain lightning }{\fs20 at other opponents.
\par }{\i\fs20 Round 3: }{\fs20 Back away from first opponent and use }{\i\fs20 maze }{\fs20 or }{\i\fs20 meteor swarm }{\fs20 on any spellcaster causing trouble.
\par }{\i\fs20 Round 4: }{\fs20 Sunder the weapon of the next most effective combatant, or use }{\i\fs20 greater dispel magic }{\fs20 on all nearby opponents.
\par }{\i\fs20 Round 5: }{\fs20 Full attack against any nearby opponent, or use }{\i\fs20 fire storm}{\fs20 .
\par Use another quickened }{\i\fs20 chain lightning }{\fs20 if foes seem really dangerous.
\par A titan usually reserves its }{\i\fs20 gate }{\fs20 and }{\i\fs20 etherealness }{\fs20 abilities to escape a fight that is not going well.
\par }{\fs36 
